ayment services; software solutions; hardware products, such as registers, terminals, stands, and readers for contactless and chips; banking services consisting of lending, instant transfer, and checking and savings accounts; and full-service setup and support services. This segment also provides loyalty, marketing, team management, and payroll services; and gift cards. It also offers Square Handheld, a portable point-of sale device for transaction purposes. The Cash App segment offers financial tools, including peer-to-peer payments, bitcoin, and stock investment brokerage; Cash App Card, a debit card; Cash App Pay, mobile-friendly way for cash app customers to pay at merchants across online and in-person channels; direct deposit, stock brokerage, and tax preparation services; and Afterpay, a buy now, pay later platform. In addition, the company operates TIDAL, a platform for musicians and fans; TBD, an open developer platform focused on making the decentralized financial world accessible; Bitkey, a self-custody bitcoin wallet; and proto. The company was formerly known as Square, Inc. and changed its name to Block, Inc. in December 2021. Block, Inc. was incorporated in 2009 and is based in Oakland, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jack  Dorsey | Co-Founder, Block Head & Chairman | Age 48 | Compensation: $3 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $2.4M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 34%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $238K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $119K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Block, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $47.0B market cap on $24.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 13% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 36%.","The business throws off $2.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.98\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 6.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 5.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 41% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4067105172506555},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $21.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PROPEL Center Names University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff Winner of the Future of XYZ HBCU Innovation Challenge at AfroTech","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/propel-center-names-university-of-arkansas-at-pine-bluff-winner-of-the-future-of-xyz-hbcu-innovation-challenge-at-afrotech-302950680.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795786980.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.923,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Block (XYZ) Launches Squaremates As Fair Value Debate Comes Back Into Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-xyz/block/news/block-xyz-launches-squaremates-as-fair-value-debate-comes-ba","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795695151.232,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"Block (XYZ) Opens Squaremates To U.S. Sellers With Deeper AI Task Automation","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/block-xyz-opens-squaremates-u-181311387.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795630391.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Block, Inc. Reaches $442.5 Million Agreement to Settle Federal Securities Class Action","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/block-inc-reaches-4425-million-agreement-to-settle-federal-securities-class-action","date":"